# JDT: refresh workspace after Maven / SB3 changes

Whenever any `pom.xml` is edited (or other Maven model files this project uses), or after you run tests or builds with the `sb3` profile (e.g. `./mvnw clean test -Psb3`, `./mvnw clean install -Psb3`), you **must** refresh the JDT workspace so Eclipse and the `jdt` CLI see the same classpath and test sources as Maven.

Run, from the repo root (this is Eclipse **Maven › Update Project**, Alt+F5, not a plain incremental build):

```bash
jdt maven update --project spring-data-expresspecs -f
jdt problems --project spring-data-expresspecs
```

`jdt maven update` re-reads the POM and refreshes the M2E project configuration; `-f` waits for the auto-build to finish. Then use `jdt problems` to confirm there are no compilation errors.

Do **not** substitute `jdt build` for this step when the goal is to sync from Maven after a POM or `sb3` classpath change—only `jdt maven update` applies the POM to the workspace.
